    kind: work_item  # 426c
    title: "Tracker CLI: batch mutation command with deferred auto-sync"  # 426c
    status: needs_human_review  # 426c
    priority: 2  # 426c
    parent:  # 426c
    tags:  # 426c
    - tracker  # 426c
    - cli  # 426c
    before: []  # 426c
    duplicate_of: []  # 426c
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 426c
    pr_ref:  # 426c
    description: "## Problem\n\nWhen multiple tracker mutations are chained in a single shell invocation (cmd1 && cmd2 && cmd3),\nauto-sync can fire mid-batch when pending ops exceed the 40-line threshold. Auto-sync is\nsynchronous and blocking (push, poll CI, merge) — typically 5-15 minutes. Remaining commands\nin the chain stall silently.\n\n## Design\n\nA `tracker batch` subcommand that accepts multiple individual operations:\n\n1. Each op is individually atomic — it either fully applies or fully fails\n2. Local validation runs after each op against compiled state that includes prior ops in the batch\n   (so `add X` then `update X --add-before Y` works)\n3. Auto-sync is suppressed between ops — fires once at the end\n4. Exit code 0 ONLY if all ops AND the final auto-sync succeed\n5. If ANYTHING fails (any op or the sync), return non-zero with a per-op result report\n   listing each operation and whether it succeeded or failed\n\n## Input format\n\nTBD — options include:\n- Heredoc/stdin (one command per line)\n- Repeated --op flags\n- A YAML/JSON manifest file\n\n## What this is NOT\n\n- NOT all-or-nothing batch atomicity — if op #3 fails, ops #1 and #2 stand\n- NOT a transaction with rollback — ops are append-only, rollback is architecturally wrong\n- The batch is a sequence of individually-atomic operations with deferred sync\n\n## Root cause\n\n_maybe_auto_sync() in cli.py:1731-1736 fires after EVERY mutation command. No mechanism exists\nto group mutations and defer sync. The CI poll in do_sync() blocks for 5+ minutes."  # 426c
    fields: {}  # 426c
